WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.110
Leave the food and go.

3
00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:28.197
My uncle says I must beg your
forgiveness for deceiving you.

4
00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.856
Your uncle?

5
00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.316
Prince baelor.

6
00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.010
The heir to the iron throne.

7
00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.946
- I never meant to lie.
- Yeah. but you did.

8
00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.866
About everything.
starting with your name.

9
00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:43.706
I've not heard of a prince egg.

10
00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:46.166
- Short for aegon.
- Of course.

11
00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:47.650
After the conqueror?

12
00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.376
How many aegons have been king?

13
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.200
Four. Four aegons.

14
00:01:58.870 --> 00:01:59.870
So why'd you do it?

15
00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:02.710
Was it some jape?

16
00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.960
Make a fool of the stupid hedge knight?

17
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.606
No. I was supposed to squire for daeron.

18
00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.050
He's my older brother.

19
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.776
He's a shit knight. and a drunk.

20
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.720
And he didn't want to enter the lists.

21
00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.496
He only meant for us to hide in
that inn until the tourney was over.

22
00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.246
- You shaved your head.
- It was daeron who shaved it.

23
00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.270
Was it daeron that told
me you were a stable boy?

24
00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.070
- I didn't...
- what?

25
00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.716
I didn't think I was doing anything wrong.

26
00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:34.450
Of course. you did.

27
00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:36.870
That's why you lied.

28
00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.000
Dry your eyes.

29
00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.566
I was just so disappointed
when I couldn't go to the tourney...

30
00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:51.550
we can't have the little prince
being disappointed now. can we?

31
00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.606
I just wanted to be
somebody's squire. ser.

32
00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.380
You'd have served a
donkey. were it squire-less.

33
00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.550
I'm sorry. ser.

34
00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:04.810
Truly am.

35
00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.980
It's just a bit of bad luck
we found each other. isn't it?

36
00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.870
What will they do with me. egg?

37
00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.676
My uncle wants to see
you after you're done eating.

38
00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:22.886
I'm done now. then.

39
00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.950
I've already kicked
one prince in the mouth.

40
00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.620
Don't mean to keep another one waiting.

41
00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:00.660
Rise.

42
00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.110
Pour ser Duncan a cup. aegon.

43
00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.340
Try not to spill it on him.

44
00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.340
The boy won't spill. your grace.

45
00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:18.630
He's a good boy.

46
00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:22.010
Good squire. And he meant no harm.

47
00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.866
I know that now.

48
00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.930
One need not intend harm to do it.

49
00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.166
Aegon should have
come to me when he saw

50
00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.996
what his brother was
doing to those puppeteers.

51
00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:34.836
- There was no time. uncle. i...
- instead. he ran to you. ser Duncan.

52
00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.200
That was no kindness.

53
00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.280
I wish ser Duncan had killed him.

54
00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.700
Aerion is your brother.

55
00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.330
And the septons say we
must love our brothers.

56
00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.210
Aegon. leave us now.

57
00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:56.630
As you will. your grace.

58
00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:09.730
How good a knight are you?

59
00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:12.640
How skilled at arms?

60
00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:16.860
Sir arlan taught me sword and shield and

61
00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:19.400
how to tilt at rings.

62
00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:29.830
My brother maekar returned
to the castle a few hours ago.

63
00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:35.840
He found his son daeron drunk
in an inn a day's ride to the south.

64
00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.106
- I know it.
- He told my brother

65
00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.696
that a huge robber knight
made off with aegon.

66
00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.326
I fear you have been cast
as this robber knight. ser.

67
00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:46.656
He's lying.

68
00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.496
I left that inn four nights past.

69
00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:52.366
Prince daeron did not
pursue his brother's captor.

70
00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:53.390
Seemingly not.

71
00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.666
What of the girl?

72
00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.466
By the time aerion is
done twisting the tale.

73
00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:02.700
it will be high treason.

74
00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.796
Treason? By puppetry?

75
00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:07.756
The dragon is the
sigil of the royal house.

76
00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.556
To portray one being
slain... It was surely innocent.

77
00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.436
Perhaps. but far from
wise. even in peacetime.

78
00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:16.976
Aerion calls it a veiled
attack on house Targaryen.

79
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.516
an incitement to revolt.

80
00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.380
Do you believe that. your grace?

81
00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.276
One truth is beyond dispute.

82
00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.656
You laid hands upon
the blood of the dragon.

83
00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.366
The girl's finger was snapped in half.

84
00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:32.496
No matter the cause. it is never
wise to strike a king's grandson.

85
00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:33.996
Would you not have done the same?

86
00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:35.706
I might have.

87
00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:38.020
But I'm a prince of the
realm. not a hedge knight.

88
00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:41.280
Don't all knights make the same oath?

89
00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.240
To protect the innocent?

90
00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:58.580
Aerion would like your
head for what you did to him.

91
00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:04.510
He will not have it. but I
cannot deny him a trial.

92
00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:08.696
And with daeron's accusation
that you kidnaped egg.

93
00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:10.946
the court is unlikely to rule in your favor.

94
00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:12.536
And when I'm found guilty?

95
00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:14.456
The last time a man
struck the royal blood.

96
00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:16.820
it was decreed he should
lose the offending hand.

97
00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:19.690
And you kicked him. too. did you not?

98
00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:22.520
I did.

99
00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:26.400
You have another choice.

100
00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:29.846
Whether it is a better one
or a worse. I cannot say.

101
00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:33.420
And so. I ask you
again. ser Duncan the tall.

102
00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:37.250
how good a knight are you. truly?

103
00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:08.820
Trial by combat.

104
00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:12.620
That is my right.

105
00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.160
I refuse.

106
00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:23.066
You cannot refuse.

107
00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:26.010
Any knight accused of a crime
has the right to demand as such.

108
00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.630
Unless you withdraw your claim?

109
00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:35.440
A trial of seven.

110
00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:42.076
That is my right. I do believe.

111
00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.520
What the fuck is a trial of seven?

112
00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:51.330
It is another form of trial by combat.

113
00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:56.056
Ancient. Seldom invoked.

114
00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:59.380
It came across the narrow sea
with the andals and their seven gods.

115
00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:03.250
Well. if it was the andals...

116
00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.430
I'm sorry. your grace.

117
00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.396
The old man was
never much for praying.

118
00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:12.630
What is a trial of seven?

119
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.116
The andals believed that
if seven champions fought.

120
00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:18.770
the gods. being thus honored.
would be more like to intervene

121
00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.610
and see the guilty party punished.

122
00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:30.586
Are you cowering behind some
6.000-year-old andal foolery

123
00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:34.216
because you're afraid to
face this hedge knight alone?

124
00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.740
- No.
- Then why?

125
00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.780
Why not slay the rogue yourself?

126
00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.607
Daeron has been wronged as well.

127
00:09:43.631 --> 00:09:47.436
Ser Duncan must pay for each
one of his crimes against us.

128
00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:51.146
Or would we leave a matter
of Targaryen honor in doubt?

129
00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:53.156
Do not speak to me of honor. boy.

130
00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:55.156
This is fucking nonsense.

131
00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:56.350
Is it?

132
00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.340
No.

133
00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.980
Aerion is within his
rights. We have no choice.

134
00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:13.836
A trial of seven must be held at dawn.

135
00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.006
What does that mean?
That I must fight seven men?

136
00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:18.636
Do not play the fool.

137
00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.500
It must be seven against seven.

138
00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.726
You must find six other
knights to fight beside you.

139
00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:25.266
But I have no one else.

140
00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:28.540
If a cause is just.
good men will fight for it.

141
00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.920
If not. it will be because you are guilty.

142
00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:44.900
Come here.

143
00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.690
Idiot!

144
00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.740
Can I go now?

145
00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:10.330
Seek your champions. ser Duncan.

146
00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:43.120
Lads.

147
00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.170
I've mucked it up this time.

148
00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:51.000
- I think I'm gonna die tomorrow.
- Dunk!

149
00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:54.340
Is that you? You're alive.

150
00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:03.810
Raymun. thank you for
watching my... are you hungry?

151
00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:06.600
- No. not really.
- Come on.

152
00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:11.086
- Whoa!
- Were you talking to your horses?

153
00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:13.740
- Yeah.
- That's fucking mad.

154
00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:17.046
Trial of seven.

155
00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:21.096
Duncan. that means battleaxes.
morning stars. and lances of war.

156
00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.176
- I know what it means.
- I apologize.

157
00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.346
Seems cousin here has milk in his veins.

158
00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:28.186
- Fuck off. I just meant...
- this is knightly combat. raymun.

159
00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:30.630
As you are no knight.
your skin is not at risk.

160
00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:36.540
I saw what aerion did
to those puppeteers.

161
00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:39.590
All knights vow to protect the innocent.

162
00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:41.300
Even hedge knights. I assume.

163
00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:45.600
I'm for you.

164
00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:50.900
Thank you. ser.

165
00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:57.416
- Perhaps you shouldn't.
- It pains me to admit it.

166
00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:58.916
but steffon's a fine sword.

167
00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:01.230
- Why would that pain you?
- I don't doubt that.

168
00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:04.517
But the dragon house will not look
kindly on those who oppose them.

169
00:13:04.541 --> 00:13:05.870
Dragon house?

170
00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.750
Where are their dragons. ser Duncan?

171
00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.062
Us fossoways. we were here

172
00:13:12.086 --> 00:13:14.606
long before these others
come to our shores.

173
00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:16.870
And I'll warrant we'll be
here long after they are gone.

174
00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:21.640
- Who else fights with us?
- I know no one else.

175
00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:26.130
I'm sure we can find five more good men
who wish singers to make them immortal.

176
00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:31.230
I do not know why tragedy so
oft follows after honorable men.

177
00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:34.496
But when I find myself
without the answers.

178
00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:36.980
the answer is always "more glory."

179
00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.926
Lucky for you. I have some friends.

180
00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:42.966
Ser lyonel. lord Lannister. ser otho.

181
00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:45.096
They won't be happy at being woken.

182
00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:46.760
Then they'll fight like pestered badgers.

183
00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.750
You shan't die under my watch. ser.

184
00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:52.670
I promise you that.

185
00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:20.360
Raymun. do you think your cousin
can bring the men he speaks of?

186
00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:22.740
I don't know.

187
00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:26.990
You may be wise to run.

188
00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:29.386
Won't they kill me if I run?

189
00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:30.950
Won't they kill you anyway?

190
00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:37.540
Maybe the gods figure
this is what I deserve.

191
00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:40.250
For doing what you
were supposed to do?

192
00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:44.960
For not knowing my place.

193
00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:50.260
- Ser.
- Egg!

194
00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:52.850
What are you doing?

195
00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:56.600
I'm your squire. ser. You'll
need someone to arm you.

196
00:14:58.310 --> 00:15:00.376
Does your father know
you've left the castle?

197
00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:01.860
I hope not.

198
00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:07.910
I don't think I could bear
another foot whipping tonight.

199
00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:13.386
- You!
- No! No. Duncan. no!

200
00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:15.476
Stop! Please!

201
00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:16.896
Are you mad coming here?

202
00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:19.146
I should drive this through your neck.

203
00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:20.777
I'd sooner you pour me a cup of wine.

204
00:15:20.801 --> 00:15:23.420
Fuck your wine. You lied about me.

205
00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:26.316
Well. I had to say
something when my father

206
00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:28.720
demanded to know
where egg had gotten to.

207
00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:31.390
Please. don't hurt him.

208
00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:36.520
He can't kill me twice.

209
00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:40.126
My father's going to join
the seven accusers. ser.

210
00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:43.256
Yeah. of course he will. He
must redeem his sons' honor.

211
00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:45.200
Not that I ever asked to
have my honor redeemed.

212
00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:48.176
Whoever has it can keep
it. so far as I'm concerned.

213
00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:50.540
I begged him not to. ser. I begged him.

214
00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:54.346
For what it's worth. you
have little to fear from me.

215
00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:56.556
and I'll do my best to look
gallant in the first charge.

216
00:15:56.580 --> 00:16:00.436
But after that. perhaps you
could strike me a nice blow

217
00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:02.516
to the side of the helm.

218
00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:04.276
Make it ring. Not too loud.

219
00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:06.760
Is that all you came here to say?

220
00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:12.550
My father has commanded
the kings guard to fight as well.

221
00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:17.496
Only the three that are here.

222
00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:18.940
Who do you have. ser?

223
00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:21.900
Raymun's cousin.

224
00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:30.780
I can bring people. ser. Knights. I can.

225
00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:33.636
I'll be fighting against your family.

226
00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:36.306
My father will be well guarded.
and you won't kill daeron.

227
00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:38.290
He told you he'd fall down.

228
00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:43.420
And aerion.

229
00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:45.970
You'd see him dead?

230
00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:48.606
When I was little.

231
00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:51.316
aerion used to come into
my bed chamber at night.

232
00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:53.446
put his knife in between my legs.

233
00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:55.576
He had too many brothers. he'd say.

234
00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:58.520
Maybe one night. he'd make me
his sister. Then he could marry me.

235
00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:06.006
Sorry. that was... Egg has the truth of it.

236
00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:07.796
Aerion can be quite the monster.

237
00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:10.006
And he threw my cat in the well. too.

238
00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:12.620
- He says he didn't. but he did.
- Alright.

239
00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:17.016
He thinks he's a dragon in human form.

240
00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.687
That's why he was so
wroth at the puppet show.

241
00:17:18.711 --> 00:17:20.726
A pity he wasn't born a fossoway.

242
00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:23.230
Then he'd think himself an
apple and we'd all be a deal safer.

243
00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:27.160
I must steal back to the castle.

244
00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.300
Ser Duncan?

245
00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:31.380
Private word?

246
00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:51.610
I dreamed of you.

247
00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:54.610
You said that.

248
00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:58.410
- At the inn.
- Did I?

249
00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:03.040
Well. my dreams are not like yours.

250
00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:05.630
Mine come true.

251
00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:09.896
An impressive talent
for an unimpressive man.

252
00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.630
Another one of life's little ironies.

253
00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:15.640
But I have seen you. ser.

254
00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.100
And a fire.

255
00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:20.810
And a dead dragon.

256
00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:28.190
A great beast with wings so
large they could cover this Meadow.

257
00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.506
It had fallen on top of you.

258
00:18:31.530 --> 00:18:34.660
But you were alive. and
the dragon was dead.

259
00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:39.240
Did I kill it?

260
00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.870
That I could not say.

261
00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:47.660
We were dragon masters once.

262
00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:51.856
Hard to believe.

263
00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:53.840
Now. they're all gone. but we remain.

264
00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:58.930
I don't care to die today.

265
00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:03.350
I don't care to die either.

266
00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:10.257
It may be that I've killed you with my lie.

267
00:19:10.281 --> 00:19:12.400
And if so. I'm sorry.

268
00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.610
I'm doomed to some kind of hell. I know.

269
00:19:18.950 --> 00:19:20.240
Likely one without wine.

270
00:19:34.970 --> 00:19:36.760
<i>You are no knight.</i>

271
00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:49.270
You are florian the fool.

272
00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:14.800
Ser Duncan.

273
00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:19.050
If you are come for your
shield. she left it with me.

274
00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:38.690
Where did she go?

275
00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:41.700
They make for dorne.

276
00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:44.500
Well gone is well forgot.

277
00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:46.660
Good.

278
00:21:05.390 --> 00:21:06.890
Your rim was old.

279
00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:11.456
Cheap steel. Brittle and rusted.

280
00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:13.020
I've made you a new one.

281
00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:14.836
It's twice as thick.

282
00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:16.530
I've put some straps on the back.

283
00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:22.120
It will be heavier now. but stronger too.

284
00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:27.910
The girl did the paint.

285
00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:32.646
The star is fallen.

286
00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:35.970
And the sunset heralds night.

287
00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:40.130
The shield is all painted up like death.

288
00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:44.930
The elm's alive. man.

289
00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:48.366
See how green the leaves are?

290
00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:49.930
That's summer leaves. for certain.

291
00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:53.730
You remember the old shield rhyme?

292
00:21:57.320 --> 00:21:59.410
Oak and iron. guard me well.

293
00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:03.030
Or else I'm dead and doomed to hell.

294
00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:20.300
How much do you want
for the new rim and all?

295
00:22:21.970 --> 00:22:23.220
From you...

296
00:22:25.890 --> 00:22:26.970
A copper.

297
00:23:04.420 --> 00:23:05.420
Sers...

298
00:23:07.220 --> 00:23:08.486
I am in your debt.

299
00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:10.760
The debt is aerion's.

300
00:23:11.770 --> 00:23:13.150
And we mean to collect it.

301
00:23:14.350 --> 00:23:16.916
- I had heard your leg was broken.
- You heard true.

302
00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:18.860
My leg is broken. I cannot walk.

303
00:23:19.820 --> 00:23:23.160
But so long as I can sit
on a horse. I can fight.

304
00:23:23.570 --> 00:23:25.990
Ser Robyn would die
the king's faithful servant.

305
00:23:26.660 --> 00:23:30.540
But when the crown goes against the
gods. ser Robyn goes against the crown.

306
00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:33.750
I always knew you meant trouble.

307
00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:38.056
I cannot thank you enough.

308
00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:40.186
Nor ser steffon for bringing you.

309
00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:44.856
Who the fuck is ser
stevron? Your... boy found me.

310
00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:47.066
Hasn't been a trial of
seven for a hundred years.

311
00:23:47.090 --> 00:23:49.616
I wasn't about to miss a chance
to bloody up the kings guard

312
00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:51.430
in their pretty white gowns.

313
00:24:46.990 --> 00:24:49.886
Six. There are only six.

314
00:24:49.910 --> 00:24:51.846
Is it possible aerion
has not found a seventh

315
00:24:51.870 --> 00:24:53.227
to take up his claim?

316
00:24:53.251 --> 00:24:55.216
Raymun!

317
00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:56.530
My helm. if you please.

318
00:24:58.370 --> 00:25:00.500
Ser steffon. what of your friends?

319
00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:03.186
We only need one
more to make our seven.

320
00:25:03.210 --> 00:25:04.920
I'm afraid you'll need two more.

321
00:25:09.130 --> 00:25:11.420
I fight with prince
aerion and the accusers.

322
00:25:17.560 --> 00:25:18.730
No. you...

323
00:25:19.850 --> 00:25:21.326
You told ser Duncan to rely on you.

324
00:25:21.350 --> 00:25:24.206
Well. our prince would not
have made me a lord else wise.

325
00:25:24.230 --> 00:25:25.810
but for it thwarted ser Duncan.

326
00:25:29.070 --> 00:25:31.110
You traded your honor for a lordship?

327
00:25:31.950 --> 00:25:33.546
Cousin.

328
00:25:33.570 --> 00:25:36.346
I know great men who have
traded their honor for far less.

329
00:25:36.370 --> 00:25:38.460
It was a bargain well struck.

330
00:25:40.500 --> 00:25:41.920
Fetch me my horse.

331
00:25:45.420 --> 00:25:46.880
Get him yourself.

332
00:26:08.110 --> 00:26:09.740
We are lost.

333
00:26:15.370 --> 00:26:18.210
Knight me. I will take my cousin's place.

334
00:26:23.210 --> 00:26:24.670
Ser Duncan. knight me.

335
00:26:25.670 --> 00:26:27.606
Raymun. I shouldn't.

336
00:26:27.630 --> 00:26:28.880
Without me. you're only five.

337
00:26:29.920 --> 00:26:31.800
You cannot win with five.

338
00:26:33.970 --> 00:26:36.430
The lad has the truth of it. I'm afraid.

339
00:26:38.050 --> 00:26:39.996
Go on. ser Duncan.

340
00:26:40.020 --> 00:26:41.520
Any knight can make a knight.

341
00:26:56.410 --> 00:26:57.966
Go.

342
00:26:57.990 --> 00:26:59.830
I shall give squire
raymun his knighthood.

343
00:27:11.090 --> 00:27:14.890
<i>In the name of the warrior.
I charge you to be brave.</i>

344
00:27:22.270 --> 00:27:26.020
<i>In the name of the father.
I charge you to be just.</i>

345
00:27:32.070 --> 00:27:34.030
<i>In the name of the mother...</i>

346
00:27:35.030 --> 00:27:37.700
<i>I charge you to protect
the young and innocent.</i>

347
00:27:50.630 --> 00:27:51.710
Ser Duncan.

348
00:27:53.050 --> 00:27:54.390
We cannot delay any further.

349
00:27:55.050 --> 00:27:57.736
- Seems you only have five champions.
- Six.

350
00:27:57.760 --> 00:28:00.076
Ser lyonel is knighting raymun fossoway.

351
00:28:00.100 --> 00:28:01.707
We will fight you six against seven.

352
00:28:01.731 --> 00:28:03.576
I'm afraid it is not permitted.

353
00:28:03.600 --> 00:28:05.866
If you cannot find another
knight to join you. ser.

354
00:28:05.890 --> 00:28:08.020
then you must be declared
guilty of your crimes.

355
00:28:11.900 --> 00:28:13.780
M'lord. I beg a moment. please.

356
00:28:15.190 --> 00:28:16.610
You have it.

357
00:28:47.520 --> 00:28:48.730
M'lords!

358
00:28:50.770 --> 00:28:54.020
I know none of you remember
ser arlan of penny tree.

359
00:28:56.530 --> 00:28:57.990
But I was his squire.

360
00:29:00.320 --> 00:29:01.820
We served many of you.

361
00:29:04.660 --> 00:29:06.120
Ate at your tables.

362
00:29:07.250 --> 00:29:08.540
Slept in your halls.

363
00:29:14.540 --> 00:29:15.920
He was a good man.

364
00:29:18.800 --> 00:29:20.590
And he taught me how to be a knight.

365
00:29:24.430 --> 00:29:27.020
Not just sword and Lance. but honor.

366
00:29:31.140 --> 00:29:33.140
A knight defends the innocent.

367
00:29:34.520 --> 00:29:36.980
That's... that's all I did.

368
00:29:41.610 --> 00:29:46.030
I was not ser arlan's blood.
but I have followed his example.

369
00:29:47.580 --> 00:29:50.040
As your sons will follow yours.

370
00:30:02.260 --> 00:30:04.510
Who will stand and fight with me?

371
00:30:21.440 --> 00:30:22.780
The brute of bracken!

372
00:30:53.730 --> 00:30:58.400
Has courage deserted the
noble houses of Westeros?

373
00:30:59.360 --> 00:31:01.400
I will not believe it is so!

374
00:31:06.700 --> 00:31:09.240
Are there no true knights among you?!

375
00:31:33.470 --> 00:31:35.510
I will take ser Duncan's side.

376
00:31:49.120 --> 00:31:50.960
Have you taken leave of your senses?

377
00:31:52.120 --> 00:31:53.516
This man attacked my son.

378
00:31:53.540 --> 00:31:55.380
This man protected the innocent.

379
00:31:56.870 --> 00:31:58.330
As every true knight must.

380
00:31:59.250 --> 00:32:01.856
Let the gods decide if
he was right or wrong.

381
00:32:01.880 --> 00:32:02.880
Hyah!

381
00:32:03.305 --> 00:33:03.494
